WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:18.017 --> 00:19.894
Please wake up, ma'am!

00:19.978 --> 00:21.062
Doctor.

00:21.980 --> 00:22.981
I'm sleepy.

00:23.064 --> 00:25.775
No, you can't sleep! Open your eyes!

00:26.609 --> 00:27.652
It's so cold.

00:27.736 --> 00:28.695
Please hold on.

00:29.571 --> 00:31.406
Ma'am, what's your name?

00:32.615 --> 00:35.535
Seo Eun-ju.

00:36.327 --> 00:37.537
Where are we?

00:38.204 --> 00:40.123
Ma'am! What day is it today?

00:40.206 --> 00:41.416
What day is it today?

00:43.084 --> 00:45.003
Your second child was born today!
The birthday!

00:46.087 --> 00:48.965
October 16th.

00:49.048 --> 00:50.216
That's right.

00:50.800 --> 00:51.718
Please hold on.

01:00.101 --> 01:02.395
More blood, please.
And administer more FFP.

01:07.192 --> 01:09.110
CPR. Start compressions.

01:09.194 --> 01:10.445
Pack and cover the abdomen.

01:10.528 --> 01:12.197
-I need an emergency cart!
-Yes, sir!

01:12.280 --> 01:13.114
More gauze.

01:24.459 --> 01:25.460
Suction.

01:29.881 --> 01:31.090
Let's switch.

01:34.385 --> 01:35.970
A dose of epinephrine, please!

01:47.816 --> 01:52.862
You need to feed and hold your babies!

01:54.739 --> 01:57.492
You wanted to see your baby so much.

02:00.662 --> 02:02.080
Eun-ju!

02:02.705 --> 02:03.915
Honey!

02:18.221 --> 02:21.349
How can I live without you?

02:55.550 --> 02:58.761
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

02:58.845 --> 03:01.180
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

03:08.229 --> 03:09.606
Dr. Cha is on leave, right?

03:10.315 --> 03:13.735
Yeah, she was really shaken
by the death of the transferred patient.

03:14.611 --> 03:16.237
She cried for days after.

03:17.113 --> 03:18.239
It's understandable.

03:19.198 --> 03:21.534
We saw her bed being wheeled by that day.

03:21.618 --> 03:23.620
And even that glimpse
still gives me nightmares.

03:24.329 --> 03:26.205
That patient had such severe bleeding

03:26.289 --> 03:28.625
that they did a hysterectomy
and gave 30 units of blood.

03:28.708 --> 03:31.669
Once DIC set in,
there was nothing they could do.

03:31.753 --> 03:32.587
Goodness.

03:33.504 --> 03:35.590
Postpartum hemorrhage
is what I hate the most.

03:35.673 --> 03:37.342
Why do things like that even happen?

03:37.425 --> 03:39.677
Right? Why do they happen?

03:39.761 --> 03:41.554
-Hello.
-Hello.

03:41.638 --> 03:42.931
There's no way to know.

03:43.765 --> 03:48.645
Also, we can't predict in advance
if the patient will develop PPH. Right?

03:49.437 --> 03:51.689
We can't stop the bleeding from happening.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.983
So if it happens,
we must be able to deal with it.

03:54.067 --> 03:56.236
To do that, we need to study more.

03:57.320 --> 04:00.782
So for the next month,
we'll have sessions twice a week.

04:00.865 --> 04:02.659
-Professor, come on.
-Professor, come on.

04:02.742 --> 04:04.869
You sound pretty eager.
Should we make it three?

04:06.871 --> 04:12.502
This week, we'll study
what we can do when PPH does occur.

04:13.878 --> 04:14.712
What's that?

04:14.796 --> 04:17.715
They're the materials we covered
in Prof. Kong's PPH class last time.

04:23.596 --> 04:24.430
Instead of these…

04:27.850 --> 04:29.185
-Use these.
-Yes, ma'am.

04:32.730 --> 04:35.733
Okay, starting from today,
we'll be doing something very important.

04:35.817 --> 04:38.319
Instead of just theory,
hands-on, practical training.

04:38.403 --> 04:41.572
So if you doze off, sleep…

04:43.741 --> 04:45.535
or not pay attention,
I won't stand for it.

04:46.953 --> 04:47.787
Yes, ma'am.

04:51.541 --> 04:55.420
The most important thing with PPH

04:56.170 --> 04:58.715
is recognizing it right away
and acting fast.

05:00.883 --> 05:02.302
PPH?

05:02.385 --> 05:04.095
I already gave a lecture on that.

05:04.178 --> 05:06.889
-Yes.
-Then, why is Jung-min…

05:06.973 --> 05:08.850
I mean, why is Prof. Seo doing it again?

05:08.933 --> 05:11.561
Well, there was that last case.

05:11.644 --> 05:14.522
She wants to focus on practical training
for easy understanding…

05:14.605 --> 05:15.440
Easy?

05:15.523 --> 05:18.276
So what I taught last time was hard?

05:18.359 --> 05:19.193
No.

05:19.944 --> 05:22.322
As if it makes a difference
if she does it.

05:23.031 --> 05:24.657
She thinks she can do it all.

05:24.741 --> 05:26.993
God, she's so arrogant.

05:29.454 --> 05:31.414
Our surgery's at 3:00 p.m., right?

05:31.497 --> 05:32.498
Well…

05:33.082 --> 05:36.961
Prof. Seo has six surgeries today,
and she did an emergency C-section.

05:37.920 --> 05:40.506
And spinal anesthesia failed
in a different surgery,

05:40.590 --> 05:43.342
so they said switching
to general anesthesia delayed things.

05:43.426 --> 05:45.136
So, when's mine?

05:45.219 --> 05:48.014
At around 5:00 p.m.
I've already informed the patient.

05:48.097 --> 05:49.223
What?

05:49.307 --> 05:51.768
Hey, I only have one surgery today.

05:51.851 --> 05:54.062
I'm supposed to wait
until 5:00 p.m. for one surgery?

05:55.688 --> 05:58.316
Prof. Seo has OR priority today.

05:59.650 --> 06:01.861
So she thinks she's the boss today?

06:01.944 --> 06:03.196
And can do whatever she wants?

06:04.697 --> 06:05.823
No!

06:05.907 --> 06:07.575
Ask Anesthesiology for another room.

06:08.451 --> 06:09.952
After a GS surgery,

06:10.036 --> 06:12.246
they said one might open up at 3:00 p.m.

06:13.081 --> 06:14.999
But Prof. Seo's going to use it too.

06:15.083 --> 06:16.918
If we have two, I should get one.

06:17.001 --> 06:18.252
Why does she get both?

06:19.128 --> 06:21.923
Hold on.
Is she playing mind games with me?

06:22.006 --> 06:24.342
No. She has a lot of surgeries today,

06:24.425 --> 06:26.469
so I don't think
she has the time for that…

06:29.263 --> 06:30.556
Yi-young told me

06:30.640 --> 06:34.102
she has a meeting
with the hospital director at 6:30 p.m.,

06:34.852 --> 06:38.147
so she has to be done before then
and asked for your understanding…

06:38.231 --> 06:39.649
Why is she meeting the director?

06:39.732 --> 06:41.567
That's something I don't know either.

06:41.651 --> 06:42.735
Damn it.

06:43.486 --> 06:46.030
Tell Jung-min I have to do
my surgery at 3:00 p.m.

06:46.114 --> 06:47.448
I won't do it at 5:00 p.m.

06:47.532 --> 06:49.867
And you make sure we get an OR. Okay?

06:54.956 --> 06:56.874
What do you expect me to do?

06:58.543 --> 07:01.003
Did you tell Prof. Kong
the surgeries have been delayed?

07:01.087 --> 07:01.921
Yes, I did.

07:02.004 --> 07:04.465
I notified them that
she'll do her surgery last as planned.

07:05.550 --> 07:07.468
And she agreed to it? She didn't complain?

07:08.052 --> 07:10.429
I don't know. I just need to survive.

07:14.642 --> 07:15.935
What I mean is…

07:16.018 --> 07:19.564
You said to make it
so you could leave by 6:00 p.m.

07:20.940 --> 07:24.527
But if I don't, I'll get scolded…

07:28.364 --> 07:29.407
Good job.

07:30.199 --> 07:31.200
What's gotten into you?

07:31.284 --> 07:32.410
Did something happen?

07:46.174 --> 07:49.177
Hey, next Tuesday,
I'll add an induction for Prof. Kong.

07:49.260 --> 07:52.430
You can't. Prof. Seo said
to book one for her too.

07:55.558 --> 07:58.186
Prof. Seo has three inductions on Monday.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.147
We need to do two on Tuesday.

08:01.230 --> 08:02.482
You don't have many patients.

08:03.774 --> 08:04.692
Do it on Thursday.

08:05.276 --> 08:06.486
There's a conference then.

08:06.569 --> 08:07.737
You should do it on Thursday.

08:07.820 --> 08:08.821
But Seo Jung-min…

08:10.823 --> 08:11.991
She's going too.

08:12.074 --> 08:13.409
I'm dead if I don't book Tuesday.

08:13.493 --> 08:16.037
What about Kong then?
With that temper, I'll be dead too.

08:16.120 --> 08:17.705
Damn it, this is so annoying.

08:18.498 --> 08:20.291
They should talk it out.
Why make us do it?

08:20.374 --> 08:21.542
I know, right?

08:23.127 --> 08:26.255
Hey, don't they seem weird these days?

08:26.339 --> 08:28.508
They've always been weird and still are.

08:28.591 --> 08:29.884
Well, that's true.

08:30.551 --> 08:32.261
But lately, it seems they've gotten worse.

08:32.345 --> 08:33.304
In what way?

08:33.387 --> 08:34.764
It's a bloody rivalry.

08:36.015 --> 08:36.891
So immature.

08:42.939 --> 08:46.108
I mean, one gets upset
just from hearing the name "Seo Jung-min."

08:46.192 --> 08:48.694
And the other always says no
whenever Kong Gi-sun's mentioned.

08:53.824 --> 08:55.660
And we're stuck in the middle suffering.

08:55.743 --> 08:56.827
It's ridiculous.

08:59.914 --> 09:00.873
Hi!

09:00.957 --> 09:01.791
What's going on?

09:02.375 --> 09:03.417
Why did you come back?

09:04.085 --> 09:05.753
Prof. Im's doing an emergency C-section.

09:05.836 --> 09:07.004
But you're on GYN duties.

09:07.088 --> 09:08.589
Yeah, I'm done with my GYN work.

09:08.673 --> 09:10.341
Then you should go home.

09:10.424 --> 09:11.592
Why observe an OB surgery?

09:11.676 --> 09:13.719
It's an incarceration case,
so how can I go?

09:13.803 --> 09:15.680
What do you mean "how"?
Go as fast as you can.

09:15.763 --> 09:18.641
It's a really rare case.
If not now, I may never get to see.

09:21.519 --> 09:22.520
You're really not going?

09:23.312 --> 09:24.397
We're going…

09:24.480 --> 09:25.314
Home.

09:25.398 --> 09:26.691
Okay, bye!

09:33.948 --> 09:34.991
Hello.

09:35.074 --> 09:36.200
Hey.

09:36.284 --> 09:38.160
You finished your work.
Why are you still here?

09:38.244 --> 09:39.954
There's a surgery I wanted to see.

09:42.582 --> 09:46.794
A surgery you want to see so badly
that you're staying at work?

09:46.877 --> 09:48.087
Yes.

09:49.547 --> 09:51.674
Right, it is a tough surgery.

09:51.757 --> 09:53.759
The approach is unique too.

09:53.843 --> 09:57.805
And for residents, I'm sure seeing
how the hands work will be pretty amazing.

09:57.888 --> 09:59.724
I really think it's amazing.

10:02.977 --> 10:04.270
-Gosh, you don't--
-Goodbye, sir!

10:05.062 --> 10:05.938
Where are you going?

10:06.689 --> 10:08.065
The OR changed. It's here.

10:08.149 --> 10:09.108
No, it's not.

10:09.650 --> 10:11.319
Dr. Im's C-section is in OR 6.

10:13.904 --> 10:16.782
Hey, you're on GYN rotation now.

10:16.866 --> 10:19.869
Yes, but they say incarcerations
are unique right from the incision,

10:19.952 --> 10:21.037
so I really want to see it.

10:23.080 --> 10:24.165
See you tomorrow, sir.

10:29.712 --> 10:30.630
Goodness.

10:32.548 --> 10:34.258
She is just hopeless.

10:39.263 --> 10:40.097
Hey!

10:41.599 --> 10:43.726
Why did you call me?
You're not even ready!

10:46.520 --> 10:48.230
Maybe I should've observed too?

10:48.314 --> 10:49.649
You said you had plans.

10:49.732 --> 10:52.276
Who cares?
They said it's a really rare case.

10:53.027 --> 10:55.905
Incarcer… round?

10:55.988 --> 10:58.157
-Incarceration.
-Right. That.

10:58.741 --> 11:00.409
Are you sure you want to see it?

11:00.493 --> 11:01.744
Right?

11:01.827 --> 11:05.206
You sure you want to see
the surgery and not the Hello Girl?

11:05.289 --> 11:07.375
What are you saying?
Why would I want to see her?

11:07.458 --> 11:11.087
I mean, you've been following
Sa-bi everywhere lately.

11:11.170 --> 11:13.214
-I was just wondering.
-When?

11:13.297 --> 11:14.965
The whole time ever since karaoke night.

11:15.049 --> 11:15.925
Yeah.

11:16.550 --> 11:20.471
I mean, October's almost gone,
and we're almost second-years now.

11:21.597 --> 11:23.766
When you're around Sa-bi,
you learn things.

11:23.849 --> 11:25.393
And she's good at explaining things.

11:25.476 --> 11:26.769
She makes it easy to understand.

11:26.852 --> 11:27.937
Whatever.

11:28.771 --> 11:31.482
If you two end up dating,
you have to tell us first.

11:32.108 --> 11:34.652
After all,
we spend 16 hours a day together.

11:34.735 --> 11:36.362
It would hurt to find out secondhand.

11:36.445 --> 11:37.279
KU DO-WON

11:37.363 --> 11:38.322
You're spinning tales, geez.

11:43.828 --> 11:44.662
Hello?

11:46.163 --> 11:46.997
I'm at the hospital…

11:49.333 --> 11:50.167
Sure, I'd…

11:51.627 --> 11:52.461
Sounds good.

11:53.963 --> 11:54.797
Okay, bye.

11:59.468 --> 12:00.302
Who was that?

12:00.386 --> 12:01.429
Are you…

12:02.054 --> 12:03.806
It was my brother-in-law.

12:04.473 --> 12:07.017
He was passing by and is giving me a ride.

12:08.018 --> 12:10.312
Then can you give me
a ride to the bus stop?

12:10.396 --> 12:11.689
It's in the same direction.

12:11.772 --> 12:12.898
Hey, me too.

12:12.982 --> 12:14.775
And I can greet your brother-in-law too.

12:14.859 --> 12:16.527
-No!
-Hey.

12:16.610 --> 12:17.611
Why not?

12:18.154 --> 12:18.988
You can't.

12:19.488 --> 12:20.823
We have things to talk about.

12:21.574 --> 12:22.575
It's family stuff.

12:22.658 --> 12:23.909
Okay, I'll cover my ears then.

12:24.618 --> 12:25.536
Yeah, me too.

12:25.619 --> 12:26.495
No!

12:26.579 --> 12:30.082
Come on. I'm too weak to even walk.

12:30.166 --> 12:31.000
No, no.

12:31.083 --> 12:32.460
Why is everything a "no"?

12:34.295 --> 12:35.129
He's…

12:36.672 --> 12:37.506
very shy.

12:38.466 --> 12:40.885
He hates riding
with people he doesn't know.

12:42.261 --> 12:43.971
I'll give you a ride next time.

12:44.847 --> 12:45.764
Go on.

12:47.308 --> 12:48.392
Yi-young, you're…

12:50.895 --> 12:51.729
so mean.

12:52.855 --> 12:53.814
Bye!

12:54.899 --> 12:55.733
See you tomorrow.

12:56.942 --> 12:57.818
You're mean.

13:19.924 --> 13:20.758
What?

13:21.300 --> 13:22.176
You want me to come?

13:22.968 --> 13:24.887
What? Eat?

13:25.846 --> 13:26.680
Go?

13:27.681 --> 13:28.933
I missed you too!

13:32.353 --> 13:33.521
Stay in the car?

13:34.647 --> 13:35.481
Aren't you coming?

13:36.023 --> 13:37.441
Don't do what?

13:37.942 --> 13:39.318
So you want me to stay in the car?

13:41.111 --> 13:42.112
Come on!

13:51.205 --> 13:52.623
What if someone sees?

13:55.918 --> 13:57.002
If they do, then…

13:57.586 --> 13:59.755
You said they'd assume
we're going the same way.

14:00.881 --> 14:03.133
That's because it was true then,
so it was okay.

14:03.759 --> 14:05.177
But not anymore.

14:06.595 --> 14:07.846
What do you mean?

14:07.930 --> 14:09.890
We still go the same way.

14:11.058 --> 14:12.101
No, I mean…

14:13.727 --> 14:16.397
I'm just afraid people will talk
about how we're dating.

14:16.981 --> 14:18.274
They can't know yet.

14:18.357 --> 14:19.316
Why not?

14:21.110 --> 14:24.780
Are you worried we might break up
after rumors start going around?

14:25.739 --> 14:27.867
No. We're not going to break up.

14:30.911 --> 14:34.373
It's just…
the first-years don't know anything.

14:35.499 --> 14:37.376
I wonder if I should tell them first.

14:38.502 --> 14:40.462
But where do I even begin to explain?

14:40.546 --> 14:42.548
That you were my sister's in-law,

14:43.173 --> 14:44.425
and we live in the same house?

14:44.508 --> 14:47.219
It wasn't like this at first, but now…

14:48.679 --> 14:50.931
I don't know. My head hurts. I give up.

14:51.515 --> 14:53.601
Won't they be sad
to find out secondhand later?

14:53.684 --> 14:54.727
After all, you're friends.

14:54.810 --> 14:56.020
No, we're not.

14:57.354 --> 14:58.772
They don't really like me.

15:00.190 --> 15:01.692
I don't think that's the case.

15:01.775 --> 15:03.319
Not only them,

15:04.403 --> 15:06.989
but I'm also worried people at work
will get the wrong idea.

15:07.990 --> 15:10.534
I've always made mistakes,
and I keep making them.

15:11.660 --> 15:14.038
I'm worried they'd say
it's because I'm too busy dating.

15:19.585 --> 15:21.754
I'm always being criticized, so it's fine.

15:22.838 --> 15:24.173
But I don't want it to hurt you…

15:28.177 --> 15:29.094
Do-won.

15:31.972 --> 15:32.806
Sorry?

15:34.141 --> 15:35.309
What?

15:36.393 --> 15:37.394
What?

15:37.478 --> 15:38.437
It's your name.

15:39.104 --> 15:40.105
Do-won.

15:43.275 --> 15:46.320
Well, that is true. You're right. Yes.

15:46.403 --> 15:47.237
"Yes"?

15:47.821 --> 15:48.906
Don't say, "Yes."

15:49.531 --> 15:50.658
Be casual and say, "Yeah."

15:55.704 --> 15:56.664
It's still a bit…

15:56.747 --> 15:59.917
At work, you go, "Hey, Yi-young,"
and have no trouble being casual.

16:00.000 --> 16:00.834
You're right.

16:01.794 --> 16:02.628
Then…

16:04.254 --> 16:05.130
Well…

16:05.673 --> 16:06.507
Yi…

16:14.640 --> 16:15.474
Oh Yi-young…

16:17.935 --> 16:19.645
Dr. Oh. I can't do it!

16:22.398 --> 16:24.650
Let's just go home, Do-won.

16:34.034 --> 16:35.703
OH YI-YOUNG
WANT TO GO FOR A WALK?

16:37.204 --> 16:39.665
KU DO-WON
SOUNDS GOOD

16:39.748 --> 16:41.583
-Hey.
-What?

16:41.667 --> 16:42.626
Are you seeing someone?

16:43.752 --> 16:44.586
What?

16:46.755 --> 16:47.881
No.

16:53.095 --> 16:53.929
Yeah.

16:54.013 --> 16:54.847
-What?
-What?

16:54.930 --> 16:56.348
-What?
-Holy cow!

16:56.432 --> 16:57.850
I knew it.

16:57.933 --> 17:00.894
You've been staring at your phone all day.

17:00.978 --> 17:03.022
Hey, either sit down properly or get lost.

17:03.105 --> 17:04.148
Who is it?

17:05.774 --> 17:07.026
Is it someone from work?

17:08.235 --> 17:09.987
Oh, my. Did you know too, Do-won?

17:10.070 --> 17:11.530
No. What?

17:12.948 --> 17:14.033
There's no way he'd know.

17:14.116 --> 17:15.659
He's not interested in such things.

17:15.743 --> 17:16.577
Who is it?

17:16.660 --> 17:18.579
Forget it. Whatever. Don't date.

17:18.662 --> 17:19.913
-Why not?
-What?

17:22.166 --> 17:25.044
Well, it obviously
sounds like a colleague.

17:25.127 --> 17:28.714
If they break up in the end,
I'm just worried it'd cause a mess.

17:28.797 --> 17:31.300
She's terribly fickle.

17:31.383 --> 17:34.678
One minute she's in love,
the next minute she's not.

17:35.846 --> 17:36.930
When was I ever like that?

17:37.014 --> 17:39.308
And I've never dated anyone before.

17:39.892 --> 17:40.893
This is my first love.

17:40.976 --> 17:41.977
Oh, my God!

17:43.520 --> 17:45.355
Won-woo, Sang-min,

17:45.939 --> 17:47.900
and who else was it?

17:47.983 --> 17:49.610
Was it Hoo-ni?

17:50.152 --> 17:51.820
Or was it So-ni?

17:51.904 --> 17:53.113
Anyway, don't you remember?

17:53.697 --> 17:55.741
No, I've never heard of them before.

17:55.824 --> 17:57.034
Who are they?

17:57.117 --> 18:01.747
Anyway, don't be foolish with dating
and inconvenience your coworkers.

18:01.830 --> 18:03.999
You have to see them
every day for four years.

18:04.083 --> 18:06.877
Right. That's why they say
dating a coworker, a friend,

18:06.960 --> 18:09.963
or someone with complicated ties
is a bad idea.

18:10.756 --> 18:12.174
You and Joo-young were coworkers.

18:12.257 --> 18:14.176
If you get married like us,
then it's okay.

18:14.927 --> 18:15.928
We will.

18:16.011 --> 18:17.096
Oh, my gosh!

18:18.347 --> 18:20.891
What am I, a vegetable that needs water?

18:21.517 --> 18:22.351
Gross.

18:22.893 --> 18:24.353
But wait, what did you say?

18:24.436 --> 18:26.396
What are you going to do? Get married?

18:26.480 --> 18:27.439
You?

18:29.817 --> 18:30.859
For goodness' sake.

18:30.943 --> 18:33.987
Then show me.
I'll be at the hospital in a couple days.

18:34.071 --> 18:35.405
Introduce us to him.

18:42.538 --> 18:44.873
I was just joking.
It was to make you laugh.

18:44.957 --> 18:46.458
For crying out loud.

18:47.042 --> 18:50.629
Hey. If it was a joke,
why did you make it sound so serious?

18:50.712 --> 18:51.797
Why are you so angry?

18:51.880 --> 18:53.048
I'm not!

18:56.844 --> 18:58.470
Don't treat me like those bean sprouts!

18:58.554 --> 19:00.180
What's wrong with this one?

19:00.764 --> 19:02.015
Give her some slack.

19:02.099 --> 19:05.227
The day after tomorrow is
the third blood test, and she's nervous.

19:05.310 --> 19:07.521
What are you talking about? I'm fine.

19:08.272 --> 19:09.273
I'm not nervous at all.

19:10.941 --> 19:13.944
Results of the first test were ambiguous,
so they did a second one.

19:14.528 --> 19:16.238
They showed an ambiguous increase too.

19:16.321 --> 19:19.324
They said the third test
should be at least double the second.

19:19.408 --> 19:20.284
But I'm not sure.

19:20.868 --> 19:23.287
Still, the pregnancy tests
consistently showed two lines.

19:23.370 --> 19:26.039
It was like that during the third round
of IVF and still failed.

19:27.040 --> 19:28.041
Don't get your hopes up.

19:28.125 --> 19:29.501
Okay, I won't.

19:30.169 --> 19:31.628
We're doing it one more time anyway.

19:31.712 --> 19:34.464
So if it works, great.
If not, what can we do?

19:34.548 --> 19:35.507
Right.

19:35.591 --> 19:37.968
I almost forgot.
I can't make it to the hospital that day.

19:38.051 --> 19:40.053
Can one of you come? Please?

19:40.637 --> 19:41.555
I'll see if I can.

19:41.638 --> 19:43.265
I'm surprised. You must be really busy.

19:43.891 --> 19:46.393
He's been doing a research project
with nanoparticles,

19:46.476 --> 19:48.937
and it reached deterministic
and statistical optimization.

19:49.021 --> 19:51.315
What has done what?

19:51.398 --> 19:52.858
They're called nanoparticles,

19:52.941 --> 19:54.818
and their surface-modifying
polymer coating…

19:54.902 --> 19:56.361
Look, you wouldn't know.

19:57.237 --> 19:58.989
You know who started that research?

19:59.573 --> 20:02.576
My predecessor and researcher,
Oh Joo-young.

20:02.659 --> 20:05.245
Gosh, before I quit,

20:05.329 --> 20:08.373
that was my prized research project.

20:11.835 --> 20:13.170
And all this time,

20:14.504 --> 20:15.756
what have I been doing?

20:19.384 --> 20:21.303
No, what I mean is

20:21.845 --> 20:23.931
my work's a part of it too,

20:24.014 --> 20:25.557
so I want you to do your best with it.

20:26.141 --> 20:28.393
Of course. Everything will work out
for the both of us.

20:30.187 --> 20:31.939
I said not to get your hopes up.

20:32.022 --> 20:32.940
Okay.

20:45.494 --> 20:47.204
-I'll take it!
-I'll take it!

20:47.788 --> 20:48.789
It's Prof. Seo's patient.

20:48.872 --> 20:49.706
Hold on.

20:49.790 --> 20:51.208
Professor Kong said--

20:51.291 --> 20:53.210
Be quiet. You'll wake the babies.

20:56.296 --> 20:59.299
I'm fine either way, so you two
come to an agreement and let me know.

21:01.385 --> 21:02.970
Gosh, they're always bickering.

21:06.473 --> 21:09.393
Ms. Na Hyo-jin. At 33-weeks
and in MFICU with preeclampsia.

21:10.310 --> 21:11.645
Her BP had been stable,

21:11.728 --> 21:15.065
but it rose to 150 this morning,
and she now has a headache.

21:15.732 --> 21:16.858
She needs to deliver today.

21:17.484 --> 21:19.987
Chae Yu-ra. At 33-weeks
and in MFICU with PPROM.

21:20.070 --> 21:21.947
She developed a fever this morning.

21:22.030 --> 21:24.449
She has to deliver today,
but EBW's only 1,900 g.

21:24.533 --> 21:25.367
Really?

21:25.450 --> 21:26.994
Our baby's 1,800 g.

21:27.077 --> 21:28.996
It's smaller and more delicate.

21:29.079 --> 21:31.331
Our patient might have chorioamnionitis.

21:31.415 --> 21:33.166
Ours might develop preeclampsia.

21:33.250 --> 21:34.626
Just transfer your patient.

21:34.710 --> 21:35.919
-I said no.
-I can't either.

21:36.003 --> 21:37.337
-This is Pediatrics.
-If I do,

21:37.421 --> 21:38.922
-Kong wants me gone.
-Yes, I'm coming.

21:39.006 --> 21:40.090
Then go!

21:42.509 --> 21:44.136
-Wait, why?
-Where are you going?

21:44.219 --> 21:46.305
Dr. Myeong's in delivery,
but the baby's not well.

21:47.180 --> 21:48.015
Move.

21:50.684 --> 21:51.643
Watch your feet.

21:56.106 --> 21:59.109
Damn it, I just got robbed.

22:01.069 --> 22:02.821
I'd like it if you could come and check.

22:03.822 --> 22:06.575
My mom's IV is leaking again.

22:07.242 --> 22:08.285
Okay, we'll check.

22:10.037 --> 22:10.871
Thank you.

22:17.753 --> 22:21.089
Wait, isn't that the guardian
who made a scene

22:21.173 --> 22:22.841
for poking his mother twice with the IV?

22:22.924 --> 22:24.009
Yes, that's him.

22:24.092 --> 22:26.094
I'm surprised he said thank you.

22:27.346 --> 22:29.139
Last time they were admitted,

22:29.222 --> 22:32.976
the professor exploded at him
for calling me "lady."

22:33.935 --> 22:36.563
After that, he's been kind.
It's just his tone.

22:36.646 --> 22:38.440
-I'll go check.
-Okay.

22:41.068 --> 22:43.528
Hey, what have you been doing?
The patient's burning up!

22:45.781 --> 22:46.656
Is that…

22:47.157 --> 22:49.701
It's POD 1, so we did a chest X-ray.

22:49.785 --> 22:51.411
It looked fine, so we're observing them.

22:51.495 --> 22:52.829
Even if that was fine,

22:52.913 --> 22:55.665
if the patient keeps getting a fever,
you have to do something!

22:55.749 --> 22:59.920
Blood and urine cultures
are taken on POD 2 and 3.

23:00.587 --> 23:04.674
And the wound culture is done
on POD 4 and 5 if there's a fever.

23:05.884 --> 23:09.262
I was going to check the wound
during the routine dressing tomorrow.

23:09.346 --> 23:11.932
Hey, are you giving me a lecture?

23:12.724 --> 23:14.142
-No.
-I told you.

23:14.226 --> 23:17.062
Only tell me things I don't know.

23:17.145 --> 23:19.981
Don't waste your breath
on things I already know!

23:21.983 --> 23:22.984
I'm sorry.

23:23.068 --> 23:27.114
I don't care what POD it is.
You have to find the source of the fever!

23:27.989 --> 23:28.990
So what should you do?

23:32.536 --> 23:33.662
You don't know?

23:33.745 --> 23:34.663
I do.

23:34.746 --> 23:36.081
Then why aren't you answering?

23:38.083 --> 23:40.627
You said to only tell you things
you don't know…

23:42.671 --> 23:44.381
Are you joking right now?

23:47.843 --> 23:51.555
Whether it's a blood or urine culture
or a wound complication check,

23:51.638 --> 23:54.641
get a fever workup
on the patient right now

23:54.724 --> 23:56.560
and get that temperature down, okay?

23:56.643 --> 23:58.186
Yes, Professor.

24:01.231 --> 24:03.900
I bet you wouldn't have been
this sloppy if this was OB.

24:11.575 --> 24:13.285
Why is he dragging OB into this?

24:13.368 --> 24:14.327
I don't know.

24:14.411 --> 24:17.455
Last time for a POD 1,
he complained I ran too many tests.

24:17.539 --> 24:19.082
What does he want me to do?

24:20.167 --> 24:24.337
I think you totally
got in his doghouse somehow.

24:25.547 --> 24:26.631
Did you do something wrong?

24:27.716 --> 24:28.550
Me?

24:29.718 --> 24:31.136
No, nothing.

24:33.889 --> 24:34.723
Sa-bi.

24:35.724 --> 24:37.267
This is a method I often use.

24:38.810 --> 24:40.645
If the professor's expression is

24:41.313 --> 24:43.148
bad, like really serious.

24:44.107 --> 24:46.193
Then beat them to the punch
and say, "I'm sorry!"

24:46.902 --> 24:48.486
I did nothing wrong, so why apologize?

24:48.570 --> 24:49.404
No reason.

24:50.155 --> 24:51.865
Just pretend you made a mistake and do it.

24:51.948 --> 24:53.491
But I didn't, so why pretend?

24:53.575 --> 24:54.659
What I'm saying is…

24:58.455 --> 24:59.497
Never mind.

25:00.207 --> 25:01.333
You just do it your way.

25:03.168 --> 25:04.669
I have a surgery to go to.

25:04.753 --> 25:07.339
Try not to get yelled at while I'm gone.

25:10.467 --> 25:12.510
Hey, I can't believe

25:13.303 --> 25:14.888
I'm the one saying this to you.

25:37.452 --> 25:38.370
By the way, Professor.

25:38.954 --> 25:41.164
Why didn't you do open surgery
for this cancer case?

25:44.251 --> 25:45.794
I'm not saying it was wrong.

25:45.877 --> 25:48.129
I mean, it's a complicated procedure.

25:48.213 --> 25:51.675
So I was curious about why you went
with a laparoscopic surgery instead.

25:52.300 --> 25:54.552
I'm not trying to argue at all.
I just wanted to ask.

25:54.636 --> 25:55.470
Honestly, sir.

25:58.932 --> 26:01.059
I feel so moved right now.

26:01.142 --> 26:04.271
A first-year asked me
a question during surgery.

26:04.354 --> 26:05.605
This is a first.

26:13.488 --> 26:14.698
Everyone just

26:15.657 --> 26:17.450
assumes everything we do is right.

26:17.534 --> 26:19.869
They think,
"The professor will take care of it."

26:19.953 --> 26:22.664
No one is curious like this.

26:26.334 --> 26:29.421
Studies show no difference
in patient outcomes

26:30.005 --> 26:32.340
between laparoscopy and open surgery.

26:33.508 --> 26:36.636
But in the case of this patient,

26:36.720 --> 26:38.263
she's older.

26:38.346 --> 26:40.056
So we are trying

26:40.140 --> 26:43.226
to reduce the number of hours
in surgery as much as possible.

26:44.019 --> 26:46.813
Does that answer your question…

26:47.314 --> 26:48.148
Doctor…

26:48.648 --> 26:49.566
Dr. Yoon Tae-jin?

26:50.317 --> 26:51.192
It's Um Jae-il.

26:51.276 --> 26:53.486
Yes, of course. Um Jae-il.

26:53.570 --> 26:55.739
Of course, I know you.

26:55.822 --> 26:57.782
I know about the…

26:57.866 --> 26:59.826
Hi… Hi-Man.

26:59.909 --> 27:01.411
It's HI-BOYZ.

27:02.120 --> 27:03.204
Sorry.

27:07.042 --> 27:08.168
Removing the specimen.

27:10.086 --> 27:11.087
Gosh.

27:13.757 --> 27:15.008
Look at this.

27:15.800 --> 27:17.427
Why do things like these form?

27:17.510 --> 27:20.305
They make people so upset

27:21.890 --> 27:23.391
and suffer so much.

27:24.267 --> 27:25.101
Goodness.

27:26.519 --> 27:27.354
Anyway,

27:29.105 --> 27:29.939
HI-BOYZ.

27:37.697 --> 27:38.740
You're really not going?

27:38.823 --> 27:42.118
Prof. Kong doesn't buy us pizza often.

27:42.202 --> 27:44.079
And it's from a really good place.

27:45.872 --> 27:48.541
I don't really like pizza that much.

27:48.625 --> 27:51.044
You ate a whole pie last time…

27:54.547 --> 27:56.800
I do like pizza, but today I think

27:57.634 --> 27:58.468
I have indigestion.

27:58.551 --> 27:59.511
Do you need medicine?

27:59.594 --> 28:00.720
No!

28:02.347 --> 28:03.181
I'm fine.

28:03.264 --> 28:04.808
I don't usually take drugs.

28:04.891 --> 28:06.142
You go ahead.

28:06.226 --> 28:07.268
We'll be right back then.

28:07.352 --> 28:08.311
No!

28:08.395 --> 28:09.479
No?

28:12.232 --> 28:13.650
Take your time.

28:14.234 --> 28:16.569
Eat a lot and make sure to chew carefully.

28:17.153 --> 28:18.363
You might get indigestion.

28:19.656 --> 28:21.866
-Okay. We'll be right back.
-Okay. We'll be back.

28:21.950 --> 28:23.034
I can't wait!

28:40.385 --> 28:41.970
You should've gone and eaten pizza.

28:44.264 --> 28:45.432
I like this better.

29:13.209 --> 29:14.377
Dr. Oh.

29:15.754 --> 29:17.422
I'm very confused.

29:17.505 --> 29:20.341
Do you want to keep this a secret
or tell everyone?

29:21.259 --> 29:22.469
I don't know.

29:24.804 --> 29:26.931
But I'm sure I want to be with you.

29:31.603 --> 29:32.437
Me too.

29:49.788 --> 29:51.080
I can't pick it up.

29:57.170 --> 29:59.214
-Some meat too. Yeah.
-Meat?

30:01.883 --> 30:02.717
And the spinach?

30:02.801 --> 30:03.885
Spinach too?

30:08.973 --> 30:11.184
I'm too tired to even lift my spoon.

30:12.268 --> 30:13.186
I better help you.

30:13.269 --> 30:14.521
No, Dr. Oh. No.

30:14.604 --> 30:16.648
-I'm strong.
-Really, I'm fine though.

30:23.404 --> 30:25.490
Geez, if you drop your chopsticks,

30:25.573 --> 30:26.908
pick them up…

30:28.243 --> 30:29.160
Dr. Myeong?

30:29.244 --> 30:30.411
Hello.

30:30.495 --> 30:31.329
Hi.

30:31.412 --> 30:32.831
-Dr. Oh.
-Yes?

30:32.914 --> 30:35.959
The surgery ahead of us is running long.
Bring her down 30 minutes later.

30:36.042 --> 30:37.001
Yes, ma'am.

30:42.632 --> 30:43.716
Hello, Professor.

30:44.676 --> 30:47.053
Prof. Kong wrote
the letter of recommendation.

30:48.304 --> 30:52.559
Professor applications are due next week,
so I wanted to make sure mine's in order.

30:53.351 --> 30:56.020
Yes. Thank you. Bye.

31:02.110 --> 31:03.236
Hey, Dr. Ku?

31:04.237 --> 31:05.071
By any chance,

31:05.154 --> 31:08.116
have you heard how many applied
for the professor position this time?

31:08.741 --> 31:09.576
No.

31:10.618 --> 31:12.412
I heard Dr. Yoo Jeong-hye applied.

31:12.495 --> 31:14.038
Oh, her?

31:16.207 --> 31:18.209
By the way, your lunch box…

31:22.338 --> 31:23.214
Enjoy your food.

31:23.965 --> 31:24.799
See you later.

31:24.883 --> 31:25.717
Goodbye, ma'am.

31:33.099 --> 31:33.975
Gosh, that scared me.

31:35.268 --> 31:39.022
This darn hospital is so huge,
but there's nowhere for us to date.

31:39.105 --> 31:40.899
Because dates are usually done outside.

31:40.982 --> 31:42.817
The only places we go are here and home.

31:42.901 --> 31:44.027
So when, where, and how?

31:44.986 --> 31:47.780
And at home,
we have two sets of eyes on us.

31:48.615 --> 31:49.449
Right.

31:50.241 --> 31:52.118
I have to work this weekend too.

31:52.201 --> 31:53.244
Damn it.

31:54.454 --> 31:56.456
Then want to meet
at the emergency stairs later?

31:56.539 --> 31:57.498
It's quiet there.

31:58.082 --> 31:59.459
All the floors are already full.

32:00.043 --> 32:01.586
Geez, don't they do any work?

32:04.255 --> 32:05.214
Then the elevator?

32:06.716 --> 32:08.885
You've seen too many movies.
That won't work.

32:08.968 --> 32:10.345
Then where?

32:11.679 --> 32:14.057
I have about 30 minutes after 9:00 p.m.

32:14.140 --> 32:15.433
Let's have some coffee there.

32:15.516 --> 32:17.685
-I'm sure it's empty.
-Where?

32:18.645 --> 32:19.520
It's--

32:20.897 --> 32:22.732
PYO NAM-KYUNG

32:22.815 --> 32:25.151
Damn it, she has awful timing.

32:26.486 --> 32:27.403
What?

32:31.783 --> 32:35.244
Ma'am, your cervical length looks good.
Everything's fine.

32:35.328 --> 32:37.538
You can go up to the ward now.

32:37.622 --> 32:38.998
Okay, thank you.

32:39.082 --> 32:41.417
I have to start
outpatient ultrasounds now, so move.

32:41.501 --> 32:43.002
Just one more. I swear, last one.

32:43.086 --> 32:45.129
No. Can't you see
all the patients outside?

32:45.213 --> 32:46.631
-I'll be quick.
-I said no.

32:46.714 --> 32:49.258
If they're ward patients,
use the portable ultrasound there.

32:49.342 --> 32:50.593
Why are you down here?

32:50.677 --> 32:52.762
Prof. Kong said to do
official sonographies.

32:52.845 --> 32:54.097
Look, I don't care.

32:57.433 --> 32:58.267
I'm sorry.

32:59.602 --> 33:00.436
Come on out.

33:07.902 --> 33:09.737
If ultrasounds run late,
we'll be backed up.

33:09.821 --> 33:11.739
Look, I know.

33:12.365 --> 33:15.493
But Kong had urgent decisions to make
and wanted dopplers done here too.

33:15.576 --> 33:16.828
So what am I supposed to do?

33:20.039 --> 33:20.873
It's nothing.

33:21.457 --> 33:23.126
If you take a seat here for a moment,

33:23.209 --> 33:24.419
I'll come get you soon.

33:25.294 --> 33:26.295
Okay.

33:27.755 --> 33:30.008
You should come during lunch
when we're on break.

33:30.091 --> 33:31.926
I told you several times I just heard too.

33:33.219 --> 33:35.304
Please, just this once.

33:35.388 --> 33:37.265
I have to do this fast and go back up.

33:37.348 --> 33:38.516
Damn it.

33:39.517 --> 33:40.351
Then hurry.

33:42.186 --> 33:43.062
Yes, Professor?

33:43.146 --> 33:45.023
Have you done Ms. Moon's ultrasound yet?

33:45.106 --> 33:46.899
Why isn't she here for her appointment?

33:46.983 --> 33:49.318
I'm sorry.
Ultrasounds are a bit backed up.

33:49.402 --> 33:51.154
I'll do it now and send her to you.

33:51.237 --> 33:55.116
Yi-young, outpatient care's been held up
by ultrasounds all morning.

33:55.199 --> 33:56.492
So? Do you need me to come?

33:56.576 --> 33:57.952
No, I'm sorry!

33:58.870 --> 33:59.996
I'll be quick!

34:06.210 --> 34:07.086
Hello, Professor.

34:08.588 --> 34:09.714
Yes, I checked everyone.

34:10.298 --> 34:12.508
But there's one patient
I don't think we can…

34:14.594 --> 34:16.929
No, I can do it. Yes.

34:17.805 --> 34:18.931
Yes, ma'am.

34:19.015 --> 34:19.974
Bye.

34:22.602 --> 34:24.187
Yi-young, just this once!

34:25.229 --> 34:26.314
Hello.

34:26.397 --> 34:27.565
-Hello.
-Hello.

34:28.399 --> 34:29.567
-Hello.
-Hello.

34:30.651 --> 34:31.486
Hello!

34:33.112 --> 34:34.739
Look at those bumbling fools.

34:34.822 --> 34:37.617
If they prepared beforehand,
they wouldn't need to run.

34:43.372 --> 34:44.874
What are you doing?

34:45.458 --> 34:46.584
That's hot!

35:00.223 --> 35:02.308
Ms. Jeon's surgery
is the first one for tomorrow.

35:02.391 --> 35:05.311
Did you know it's a colostomy
for bowel obstruction?

35:05.895 --> 35:07.230
-Yes, I know.
-Then tell me.

35:07.313 --> 35:09.732
Why is there porridge
when she should be fasting?

35:09.816 --> 35:11.943
Did you want the surgery to be ruined?

35:13.194 --> 35:14.028
Well…

35:14.112 --> 35:17.532
I personally asked
the chief of Surgery for this one.

35:17.615 --> 35:20.701
If this gets canceled,
how would that make me look?

35:23.329 --> 35:24.622
It's a co-op…

35:25.498 --> 35:26.999
A surgical consult--

35:27.083 --> 35:27.917
And?

35:28.501 --> 35:30.128
So what?

35:30.711 --> 35:31.921
The order

35:33.131 --> 35:34.757
by the Surgery resident…

35:34.841 --> 35:35.800
What about them?

35:36.968 --> 35:37.802
What?!

35:39.762 --> 35:40.596
I'm sorry.

35:40.680 --> 35:44.934
Hey, are you here
to save lives or to take them?

35:46.477 --> 35:48.146
Thank God I did my rounds then.

35:48.229 --> 35:49.355
But what if I hadn't?

35:50.148 --> 35:51.232
Professor Jo.

35:52.650 --> 35:53.651
Hello, Chief.

35:54.235 --> 35:55.736
Why aren't you picking up?

35:56.863 --> 35:59.740
I'm so sorry. I was just…

36:00.366 --> 36:02.743
Because of my resident…
But is something the matter?

36:02.827 --> 36:04.287
Yeah, I…

36:04.954 --> 36:06.664
Apparently, my resident made a mistake.

36:07.331 --> 36:11.460
He confused the patients
and ordered meals for Ms. Jeon.

36:11.544 --> 36:14.046
Right, the meals…

36:14.755 --> 36:17.508
You mean the porridge, right?

36:17.592 --> 36:19.302
Yeah, the porridge.

36:19.385 --> 36:21.220
Did she eat it already?

36:21.304 --> 36:23.598
-No, she hasn't.
-Goodness.

36:23.681 --> 36:25.141
There's no need to worry about that.

36:25.224 --> 36:27.018
I double-check everything.

36:27.101 --> 36:28.102
That's a relief.

36:28.769 --> 36:30.021
And you…

36:31.480 --> 36:32.523
I'm sorry.

36:35.902 --> 36:36.777
I'm sorry.

36:37.486 --> 36:39.947
It's all right.
Things like that happen often.

36:40.031 --> 36:41.449
It's okay.

36:42.241 --> 36:43.659
Just be careful from now on.

36:44.869 --> 36:47.496
Chief, since you're here,
how about we have some tea?

36:47.580 --> 36:48.623
Should we then?

36:48.706 --> 36:49.707
-Okay, let's go.
-Okay.

36:49.790 --> 36:50.708
You can go back.

37:15.775 --> 37:16.901
Why didn't you tell him?

37:19.028 --> 37:20.488
"I didn't do that."

37:22.531 --> 37:23.699
I was scared.

37:26.869 --> 37:28.454
He was in the wrong.

37:29.372 --> 37:31.040
You did nothing wrong, Dr. Kim.

37:31.123 --> 37:32.291
So chin up.

37:34.877 --> 37:35.920
Yes, sir.

37:36.003 --> 37:36.921
Hang in there.

37:38.381 --> 37:39.215
You can do…

37:42.218 --> 37:43.552
I shouldn't just say such things.

37:45.388 --> 37:48.057
I should be of some help.

37:48.140 --> 37:50.226
It's okay. Thank you.

37:51.894 --> 37:53.938
I'll put in the prescriptions.

37:54.939 --> 37:56.274
Go get yourself a coffee.

37:57.024 --> 37:57.942
It's okay, sir.

37:58.025 --> 37:59.026
No, no.

37:59.610 --> 38:01.404
Go. I want a coffee too.

38:01.487 --> 38:03.030
Hurry up. Go!

38:03.114 --> 38:04.740
Get up! Hurry!

38:04.824 --> 38:05.658
Come on.

38:05.741 --> 38:08.244
Go and get me a…

38:08.327 --> 38:11.497
You know. An iced Americano this big.

38:12.039 --> 38:12.957
You know, right?

38:16.043 --> 38:17.420
Let's see.

38:17.503 --> 38:18.671
What have we got here?

38:35.813 --> 38:36.856
Aren't you hungry?

38:42.403 --> 38:43.738
What about you?

38:46.574 --> 38:49.160
What? Is something in your coffee?
Does it taste weird?

38:49.243 --> 38:50.077
No.

38:55.958 --> 38:57.877
The cafeteria has
spicy stir-fried pork today.

38:57.960 --> 38:58.961
Really? Okay.

38:59.045 --> 39:01.505
Hey, Jae-il. Today's bunsik day.

39:01.589 --> 39:02.882
Ask her if she wants that.

39:02.965 --> 39:04.216
Ask who?

39:04.717 --> 39:06.552
Jae-il, I had bunsik yesterday.

39:06.635 --> 39:07.636
I had pork yesterday.

39:11.140 --> 39:12.016
Then, tonight--

39:12.099 --> 39:13.184
-Spicy pork.
-Bunsik.

39:15.978 --> 39:18.230
You two figure it out.
Don't put me in the middle.

39:19.440 --> 39:20.316
Did you two fight?

39:20.399 --> 39:21.525
-No!
-No!

39:21.609 --> 39:22.860
You did.

39:22.943 --> 39:24.278
Why would I? I have no reason to.

39:24.362 --> 39:26.822
Yeah, I have no reason to fight with her.

39:27.406 --> 39:29.241
But she gets me scolded a lot.

39:29.325 --> 39:30.201
You're one to talk.

39:31.118 --> 39:33.579
Sa-bi, if a patient in the ward
needs urgent care,

39:33.662 --> 39:37.166
is it that big of a deal to check her
before outpatient ultrasounds?

39:37.249 --> 39:41.045
Jae-il, can you believe some people
still don't get the outpatient process?

39:43.172 --> 39:46.926
I just wanted to have dinner.

39:50.596 --> 39:51.472
Forget it.

39:52.556 --> 39:54.558
Let's not eat and just starve together!

39:56.102 --> 39:57.436
Hey! Don't drink that!

39:57.520 --> 39:59.105
Professor Ryu bought it for me!

39:59.897 --> 40:01.065
I'm sorry!

40:03.401 --> 40:05.361
Seriously, you…

40:05.444 --> 40:06.737
Do you have to take it this far?

40:06.821 --> 40:08.906
It's not even a big deal!

40:09.615 --> 40:11.409
Damn it. I'm leaving.

40:13.119 --> 40:15.704
No one better stop me. I'm going for real!

40:16.455 --> 40:17.373
Damn it!

40:36.725 --> 40:37.893
You did great.

40:37.977 --> 40:39.770
We'll call you with the results.

40:39.854 --> 40:41.564
It'll take about an hour.

40:41.647 --> 40:44.775
I'm done with blood tests now, right?

40:44.859 --> 40:46.110
That was the last one?

40:46.193 --> 40:47.403
Probably so.

40:47.486 --> 40:48.529
Then,

40:49.447 --> 40:50.948
for next time…

40:52.616 --> 40:55.202
If the results are good,
we'll do an ultrasound next week.

40:55.286 --> 40:58.539
That's when you look at images
of the womb, right?

40:58.622 --> 40:59.582
Yes.

41:01.834 --> 41:05.004
And an hour would mean
a call at around 1:30 p.m.?

41:05.087 --> 41:07.339
We'll call you
as soon as we get the results.

41:07.923 --> 41:09.592
All right. Thank you.

41:26.317 --> 41:28.235
Dr. Oh, we have
many new patients tomorrow.

41:28.319 --> 41:31.238
Are you going to delay
the outpatient ultrasounds again?

41:31.322 --> 41:32.156
Yes, ma'am.

41:33.491 --> 41:34.867
I mean, I won't.

41:34.950 --> 41:37.661
If ultrasounds are delayed,
that's a ton of complaints.

41:37.745 --> 41:38.579
Dr. Pyo.

41:38.662 --> 41:41.582
I have 25 outpatients
who need ultrasounds tomorrow, right?

41:41.665 --> 41:42.583
Yes, ma'am.

41:42.666 --> 41:44.710
I need to be done
with my appointments by 5:00 p.m.

41:44.793 --> 41:46.504
There can't be any delays. Got it?

41:46.587 --> 41:47.963
I'll check as quickly as possible.

41:49.715 --> 41:52.259
And a room's opening up in the OB ward.

41:52.760 --> 41:53.886
I need that one.

41:54.970 --> 41:57.056
That's what I was going to say.

41:57.139 --> 41:58.182
I need it.

41:58.265 --> 42:00.351
My patient in GYN ward needs to go there.

42:00.434 --> 42:01.977
It makes doing rounds difficult.

42:02.061 --> 42:03.771
You get what I mean, Dr. Pyo?

42:03.854 --> 42:04.813
Yes, ma'am.

42:06.148 --> 42:07.066
That's what I meant.

42:07.650 --> 42:09.985
My patient's in the GYN ward too.
I'm counting on you.

42:10.528 --> 42:11.695
And make sure to eat.

42:12.321 --> 42:13.197
Yes, ma'am.

42:15.699 --> 42:16.825
Hello, Administration?

42:16.909 --> 42:18.744
I'm Dr. Pyo Nam-kyung from OB-GYN.

42:18.827 --> 42:21.038
I heard there's a room open
in the OB ward.

42:21.121 --> 42:22.122
Hey!

42:23.874 --> 42:24.959
WEDNESDAY, OCTOBER 25

42:37.680 --> 42:39.640
Sorry, I had work.

42:44.061 --> 42:45.563
Don't pretend to be nice.

42:45.646 --> 42:46.730
It's weird.

42:48.857 --> 42:50.317
They haven't called yet?

42:51.110 --> 42:51.986
No.

43:00.244 --> 43:01.078
Are you nervous?

43:02.204 --> 43:03.122
No.

43:05.874 --> 43:08.627
If it worked, it would've been
at the first blood test.

43:09.962 --> 43:11.547
I'm not getting my hopes up.

43:14.592 --> 43:15.759
Hello?

43:15.843 --> 43:17.094
Yes, this is Oh Joo-young.

43:22.891 --> 43:23.976
I see.

43:25.603 --> 43:26.812
Thank you.

43:27.855 --> 43:28.689
Goodbye.

43:43.412 --> 43:44.413
What was it at?

43:44.496 --> 43:45.456
They said 91.

43:46.290 --> 43:49.001
It was 153 during the second test.
It's even lower.

43:50.628 --> 43:51.837
A chemical miscarriage?

43:53.297 --> 43:54.131
How did you know?

43:57.134 --> 43:59.136
Right, you're a doctor.

44:02.014 --> 44:03.265
How can you laugh now?

44:05.934 --> 44:07.811
Maybe it's because I wasn't hopeful.

44:07.895 --> 44:11.023
I don't feel as bad as I thought I would.

44:14.109 --> 44:15.653
I'm fine.

44:16.487 --> 44:19.239
It's not like I heard
its heartbeat or felt a kick.

44:20.157 --> 44:21.909
It just means a cell's gone.

44:23.202 --> 44:26.538
And I still have two embryos left.

44:27.122 --> 44:28.999
It's okay. I can try again.

44:37.716 --> 44:40.135
Eat before you go. I have a bit of time.

44:42.137 --> 44:43.305
You're busy. We'll skip food.

44:44.223 --> 44:45.432
Just buy me a coffee.

44:46.892 --> 44:49.770
I couldn't have coffee because of the IVF.

44:50.896 --> 44:52.481
I could use a nice, cold one.

44:55.609 --> 44:56.443
Let's go then.

45:05.452 --> 45:06.286
And you?

45:07.788 --> 45:08.622
Iced Americano.

45:09.957 --> 45:12.960
One iced Americano
and one iced latte, please.

45:13.710 --> 45:15.170
And make the latte decaf…

45:21.552 --> 45:22.511
Never mind.

45:27.558 --> 45:28.851
It already became a habit.

45:35.941 --> 45:37.151
It was all for nothing.

45:37.818 --> 45:39.903
And I tried so hard.

45:57.296 --> 45:58.881
Come on, now.

46:04.803 --> 46:07.264
I'm sorry. One iced Americano and…

46:17.107 --> 46:19.276
an iced latte with an extra shot.

46:20.527 --> 46:21.862
With a lot of caffeine, please.

46:21.945 --> 46:22.779
Sure.

46:44.134 --> 46:46.470
PROF. JO JOON-MO

46:58.440 --> 46:59.441
Hello, Professor.

47:00.817 --> 47:02.194
Sa-bi went to the bathroom.

47:03.820 --> 47:05.364
I'll check and get right back to you.

47:05.948 --> 47:07.199
Goodbye.

47:10.160 --> 47:10.994
It was nothing.

47:11.703 --> 47:13.288
He wanted you to check the OR schedule.

47:17.918 --> 47:18.835
Did you eat?

47:20.546 --> 47:21.797
You should be at the cafeteria.

47:21.880 --> 47:24.341
What? Were you afraid
of running into the professor?

47:27.636 --> 47:28.554
Why are you here?

47:28.637 --> 47:30.305
Why else would I come to a bank?

47:30.389 --> 47:31.306
To withdraw money.

47:38.105 --> 47:40.148
They're closing now. Let's go.

47:40.732 --> 47:41.567
Okay.

47:44.611 --> 47:47.781
If you want to be alone,
come here during the day.

47:49.366 --> 47:50.576
And go there at night.

47:52.744 --> 47:53.579
Where?

47:53.662 --> 47:55.289
There's a place where no one goes.

47:56.290 --> 47:57.291
It's quiet.

48:04.214 --> 48:05.799
Don't laugh. Be quiet!

48:07.384 --> 48:08.635
Excuse me.

48:09.886 --> 48:11.305
I'll look at him. He's a friend.

48:11.888 --> 48:12.764
Sure.

48:13.390 --> 48:14.766
-Thank you.
-No problem.

48:21.023 --> 48:23.692
Do you know how hard it was
just to get here?

48:24.526 --> 48:25.527
Please help me.

48:25.611 --> 48:26.737
All right.

48:26.820 --> 48:28.947
I'll help, so stop pleading.

48:29.031 --> 48:31.116
We're friends,
so there's no need for that.

48:31.199 --> 48:33.327
I said don't laugh.

48:33.410 --> 48:34.870
Gosh, this is driving me insane.

48:41.293 --> 48:43.712
I mean, how on earth
does this even happen?

48:43.795 --> 48:45.380
There was super glue on the table.

48:45.464 --> 48:48.300
But I accidentally put my elbow on it.
So what happens?

48:48.383 --> 48:50.010
-The glue would come out, right?
-Yeah.

48:50.093 --> 48:52.429
I caught it quickly with my hands
so it wouldn't drip.

48:52.512 --> 48:53.513
And I ended up like this.

48:53.597 --> 48:55.724
If these hands are ruined,
you're out of a job.

48:55.807 --> 48:57.017
You'll be unemployed.

48:57.100 --> 48:59.895
I know, Jung-min. So please.

49:01.063 --> 49:03.440
Amen, namaste, sawasdee krub. Seriously.

49:06.276 --> 49:07.486
It's in this pocket.

49:08.278 --> 49:09.112
My goodness.

49:14.201 --> 49:15.786
It's not working. Face recognition.

49:17.746 --> 49:18.622
Okay. Wait.

49:22.834 --> 49:23.960
Darn it.

49:24.044 --> 49:25.128
For crying out loud…

49:25.712 --> 49:27.255
Damn typo.

49:31.093 --> 49:32.719
I did it!

49:32.803 --> 49:34.096
-My goodness.
-Now, put it back.

49:38.600 --> 49:39.559
Let me see.

49:39.643 --> 49:41.770
But is an obstetrician right for this?

49:41.853 --> 49:43.271
Of course.

49:44.314 --> 49:47.150
Right, we have a specialist for this.

49:47.234 --> 49:48.485
They're at our hospital now.

49:48.568 --> 49:49.778
Which department? Dermatology?

49:49.861 --> 49:51.154
Orthopedics? OEM?

49:51.238 --> 49:52.155
Not those.

49:52.239 --> 49:54.366
No, why can't you just do it instead?

49:54.449 --> 49:55.742
I'll assist you.

49:55.826 --> 49:57.202
Professor, please operate.

49:57.285 --> 49:59.413
If you get in trouble,
you should go to your hospital.

49:59.496 --> 50:00.872
Why come here and make a fuss?

50:00.956 --> 50:02.582
This is closer to my house.

50:02.666 --> 50:04.918
We'll say that
and not because you were embarrassed.

50:08.046 --> 50:09.548
The specialist is here.

50:09.631 --> 50:11.383
Who is it? Do I know them?

50:12.467 --> 50:15.053
She's the best for this.
An eminent physician.

50:15.637 --> 50:16.471
Lee Ik-jun?

50:18.682 --> 50:21.017
Weren't we meeting at the campsite?
Why are you here?

50:24.229 --> 50:25.397
And what's with your hands?

50:26.440 --> 50:27.524
What did you do?

50:31.153 --> 50:32.154
The glue…

50:33.822 --> 50:34.906
I got it on my hands.

50:34.990 --> 50:36.283
How?

50:36.867 --> 50:39.119
You know your favorite camping lantern?

50:39.202 --> 50:41.246
The handle fell off,
so I was reattaching it…

50:41.329 --> 50:43.248
For goodness' sake!

50:43.331 --> 50:45.542
I told you to leave it.

50:45.625 --> 50:47.252
Let me see. Does it hurt a lot?

50:48.003 --> 50:49.880
What are we going to do with your hands?

50:50.922 --> 50:52.466
But why are you here, Song-hwa?

50:52.549 --> 50:54.176
I told you I was revising a paper today.

50:54.676 --> 50:57.596
Chi-hong was taking a while with the data,
so I came to help.

50:57.679 --> 50:59.431
How did you know Song-hwa was here?

50:59.514 --> 51:03.852
She told me she was coming by,
so we had lunch and went up to the lab.

51:03.935 --> 51:05.812
Then I got the call
that you were in the ER.

51:07.230 --> 51:09.274
Jung-min, what should we do?

51:10.692 --> 51:13.153
Let's try warm saline first.

51:13.236 --> 51:15.906
If it doesn't work,
we'll call Orthopedics and cut them off.

51:15.989 --> 51:17.365
Hey. Geez.

51:18.909 --> 51:20.494
You sure have a lot on your hands.

51:21.328 --> 51:22.412
Ik-jun.

51:22.496 --> 51:23.663
Who's that?

51:23.747 --> 51:24.831
Ik-jun!

51:26.124 --> 51:27.125
Ik-jun!

51:28.210 --> 51:29.711
Oh, my gosh. What happened?

51:30.545 --> 51:32.214
Jung-min said you were in the ER.

51:32.923 --> 51:34.341
I was so scared.

51:37.385 --> 51:39.930
She just happened
to be in the lab when they called.

51:45.477 --> 51:46.478
How have you been,

51:47.062 --> 51:47.938
Jun?

51:48.438 --> 51:49.397
Good, of course.

51:51.942 --> 51:52.943
Are you okay?

51:53.026 --> 51:54.152
How did this happen?

51:54.653 --> 51:55.487
Well, I was…

51:56.154 --> 51:57.030
Hey.

51:57.614 --> 51:59.282
Do you only see one person here?

51:59.908 --> 52:00.867
Oh, my gosh! Song-hwa!

52:01.493 --> 52:02.786
It's been so long!

52:03.787 --> 52:04.788
How are you?

52:06.331 --> 52:07.749
You've become even prettier.

52:07.833 --> 52:09.084
Oh, stop.

52:09.167 --> 52:12.337
Right? She gets prettier every day.

52:12.921 --> 52:14.130
It's been forever, Gi-sun.

52:14.214 --> 52:16.883
You haven't changed in three years.

52:17.759 --> 52:20.345
Yeah, her looks and her skills
are exactly the same.

52:22.973 --> 52:25.433
Song-hwa, look. This is driving me crazy.

52:26.017 --> 52:27.477
-It stings.
-Does it sting a lot?

52:27.561 --> 52:29.062
It does more than sting.

52:29.145 --> 52:29.980
Wait, your hair.

52:30.647 --> 52:31.731
Geez!

52:31.815 --> 52:33.775
Stop worrying about me
and worry about yourself.

52:34.609 --> 52:35.694
What do we do?

52:36.319 --> 52:38.572
-Don't try to force them apart.
-I won't.

52:38.655 --> 52:39.489
What's going on?

52:40.574 --> 52:41.449
You didn't know?

52:42.242 --> 52:44.494
Your first love
is with Song-hwa as his last love.

52:45.078 --> 52:46.079
It's been a while.

52:46.580 --> 52:47.497
You didn't know?

52:47.581 --> 52:49.124
Stop messing around.

52:49.207 --> 52:50.584
Is that why…

52:53.003 --> 52:54.671
No, I knew too, okay?

52:54.754 --> 52:56.214
For now, you're banned from camping.

52:56.298 --> 52:57.549
Here?

52:57.632 --> 52:58.508
That hurts!

52:58.592 --> 53:00.427
Maybe wipe the lipstick
off your teeth first.

53:00.510 --> 53:01.720
This won't work.

53:03.930 --> 53:04.890
Damn it!

53:08.018 --> 53:09.394
I won.

53:09.477 --> 53:10.770
-I won.
-Hey!

53:10.854 --> 53:12.272
That's cheating if you hit like--

53:12.355 --> 53:13.523
What? Oh, right.

53:16.359 --> 53:18.194
-Did I hit too hard?
-No, it's fine.

53:18.278 --> 53:19.738
-I asked you to unstick them.
-Sorry.

53:21.448 --> 53:23.158
My goodness.

53:25.285 --> 53:29.331
If the preceding surgery runs long,
and you think mine will be delayed,

53:29.414 --> 53:32.000
you need to look for another OR yourself.

53:33.501 --> 53:36.755
If you can't even do that,
why are you here?

53:36.838 --> 53:37.964
What are you being paid for?

53:39.341 --> 53:40.300
What?

53:40.383 --> 53:43.637
Are you not interested
because it's not OB?

53:43.720 --> 53:44.930
Excuse me.

53:45.013 --> 53:47.724
Or do you not need to do well
because it's not OB?

53:47.807 --> 53:49.476
You're not an OB-GYN.

53:49.559 --> 53:51.978
I see. You're only here for OB, right?

53:52.062 --> 53:53.396
Chief!

54:00.403 --> 54:03.323
If you're going to scold her,
please stick to the OR issue.

54:03.406 --> 54:04.407
I think you can leave out

54:05.325 --> 54:08.620
all the other useless comments.

54:09.746 --> 54:10.622
Hold on.

54:11.539 --> 54:13.416
Professor Ryu, who are you talking to--

54:13.500 --> 54:14.501
Professor!

54:18.004 --> 54:21.424
I'm talking to you, Professor.

54:24.302 --> 54:25.512
If they make a mistake,

54:26.554 --> 54:27.931
of course you should scold them.

54:28.014 --> 54:28.932
But…

54:30.934 --> 54:33.061
The location and content of the reprimand

54:34.646 --> 54:36.189
still requires common courtesy.

54:43.488 --> 54:44.531
Professor Ryu,

54:44.614 --> 54:48.118
you're the one
without common courtesy right now.

54:59.087 --> 55:02.590
I mean, there's a reason
why I do this. Okay?

55:02.674 --> 55:05.176
I'm giving them
training and discipline, man!

55:05.260 --> 55:07.387
Who are you calling "man"?

55:08.430 --> 55:09.264
Also,

55:10.807 --> 55:13.101
asking questions like
why she's getting paid

55:14.019 --> 55:16.229
or assuming it's because it isn't OB

55:16.896 --> 55:19.107
isn't training or discipline at all!

55:23.028 --> 55:24.237
Dr. Kim Sa-bi

55:25.155 --> 55:27.907
already understands what she did wrong.

55:28.616 --> 55:30.076
I'm sure she does, right?

55:33.621 --> 55:34.873
That's enough, Professor.

55:43.173 --> 55:44.132
Fine.

55:45.008 --> 55:46.718
I was going to stop anyway.

55:47.302 --> 55:48.803
But why are you getting all upset?

55:48.887 --> 55:50.055
You're spoiling the mood.

55:50.138 --> 55:50.972
Goodness.

55:51.556 --> 55:52.390
Okay, I'm sorry.

55:52.474 --> 55:54.267
All right? I'm sorry.

55:54.350 --> 55:55.518
There's nothing to see here.

55:55.602 --> 55:57.604
You can get back to work, okay?

56:10.033 --> 56:10.950
Dr. Kim.

56:12.869 --> 56:13.870
Did you

56:14.913 --> 56:16.289
get an apology?

56:19.250 --> 56:20.835
I forgot to ask for that.

56:22.629 --> 56:23.463
Professor!

56:26.800 --> 56:27.717
He did.

56:29.094 --> 56:30.762
I think I heard an apology.

56:31.429 --> 56:32.514
Thank you.

56:36.267 --> 56:37.185
That's a relief then.

56:50.281 --> 56:52.200
I can't believe he did that
to a senior doctor.

56:52.283 --> 56:53.493
And in front of the juniors?

56:53.993 --> 56:55.245
What the hell?

56:59.707 --> 57:00.583
My apologies.

57:00.667 --> 57:04.212
You're not hurt, are you?
I'm a professor here.

57:04.295 --> 57:05.380
So?

57:06.673 --> 57:09.843
There's a lot of sick people here.
You should be more careful.

57:10.468 --> 57:12.637
Right. I'm sorry.

57:25.191 --> 57:27.986
I… I didn't swear.

57:31.364 --> 57:36.035
I don't yell in the hospital anymore
or talk informally to anyone.

57:36.119 --> 57:37.912
That's very good.

57:38.496 --> 57:40.999
It's so nice
to see you smiling around here.

57:42.041 --> 57:45.545
When you smile,
you show off an adorable side.

57:45.628 --> 57:46.754
-Me?
-Yes.

57:47.839 --> 57:49.132
Where were you coming from?

57:49.215 --> 57:50.341
From the ward.

57:50.967 --> 57:52.844
Your mother's improved greatly.

57:52.927 --> 57:54.304
Her lab results are good too.

57:55.305 --> 57:56.222
It's thanks to you.

57:56.306 --> 57:59.767
No, she's gotten better
because you're smiling now.

58:00.643 --> 58:02.020
All right, then.

58:02.770 --> 58:05.732
Keep on smiling.

58:05.815 --> 58:06.649
Yes, sir.

58:07.609 --> 58:08.443
-Goodbye, sir!
-Bye.

58:08.943 --> 58:10.737
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

58:21.414 --> 58:24.876
OB-GYN, OH JOO-YOUNG

58:30.381 --> 58:31.382
Pyo Nam-kyung!

58:32.425 --> 58:34.177
-Yes?
-And Oh Yi-young.

58:35.762 --> 58:37.764
Are you in a contest to see who's worse?

58:38.348 --> 58:39.891
Both of you are behind on charting.

58:39.974 --> 58:40.934
Yi-young.

58:41.017 --> 58:43.311
Birth certificates, delivery discharges,

58:43.394 --> 58:45.021
and tomorrow's discharge notes.

58:45.104 --> 58:46.272
You haven't done any of them.

58:47.398 --> 58:50.527
And Nam-kyung, you didn't write
admission notes for next week's surgeries.

58:51.110 --> 58:53.154
When are you going to
assess patients in advance?

58:53.738 --> 58:54.781
I'm sorry.

58:54.864 --> 58:56.282
I'm going in for surgery.

58:56.366 --> 58:58.952
Get that all done while I'm gone
and show me before going home.

58:59.035 --> 58:59.869
All right?

58:59.953 --> 59:02.121
I'm going to check everything.

59:03.164 --> 59:04.082
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

59:16.219 --> 59:17.053
Hello?

59:19.013 --> 59:19.847
What?

59:20.723 --> 59:23.393
Yes, I'll tell the professor right away.
Okay, bye.

59:30.525 --> 59:32.610
Ma'am, please wake up.

59:32.694 --> 59:33.528
Ma'am?

59:33.611 --> 59:35.071
Hemoglobin's 6.6.

59:35.154 --> 59:36.406
And her BP's dropping.

59:36.489 --> 59:38.241
-Squeeze the blood harder.
-Yes, sir.

59:38.324 --> 59:40.201
Ma'am? Open your eyes.

59:40.827 --> 59:43.496
Ma'am, what's your name? Ma'am.

59:43.580 --> 59:46.457
Yulje EMS HL9697.

59:46.541 --> 59:49.168
Six mile final, Yulje helipad.

59:49.252 --> 59:51.296
CENTRAL EMC

59:55.883 --> 59:56.718
Ma'am!

59:58.219 --> 59:59.220
-We're moving.
-Lift her!

59:59.304 --> 01:00:00.680
-One, two, three!
-We're moving.

01:00:02.432 --> 01:00:04.100
One, two, three!

01:00:05.852 --> 01:00:07.979
She delivered via precipitous labor
two hours ago.

01:00:08.062 --> 01:00:10.857
We did a balloon tamponade for PPH,
but she keeps bleeding.

01:00:10.940 --> 01:00:12.692
BP dropped to 70 over 40.

01:00:12.775 --> 01:00:13.735
Now it's 90 over 60.

01:00:13.818 --> 01:00:15.945
First unit given was universal O.

01:00:16.029 --> 01:00:18.281
She had DDLT surgery seven years ago.

01:00:18.364 --> 01:00:21.326
Ma'am! Please wake up! Ma'am!

01:00:21.409 --> 01:00:23.620
Let's get her to the ER
and secure a line first.

01:00:23.703 --> 01:00:25.038
Then take her up to the OR.

01:00:28.374 --> 01:00:30.418
Connect the monitors and check her vitals.

01:00:30.501 --> 01:00:32.086
-Yes, sir.
-Please bring the ultrasound.

01:00:32.170 --> 01:00:33.004
Yes, Doctor.

01:00:37.425 --> 01:00:38.718
-Placing a central line.
-Okay.

01:00:44.390 --> 01:00:45.224
Pyo Nam-kyung!

01:00:47.393 --> 01:00:48.269
Pyo Nam-kyung!

01:00:49.520 --> 01:00:51.147
Hey, Nam-kyung!

01:00:52.690 --> 01:00:53.608
Yi-young.

01:00:54.192 --> 01:00:55.735
We have to quickly…

01:00:55.818 --> 01:00:57.612
I don't think I can do it.

01:00:58.196 --> 01:00:59.113
I don't know.

01:00:59.197 --> 01:01:00.531
There's no time for that.

01:01:01.532 --> 01:01:02.617
She's bleeding!

01:01:04.452 --> 01:01:05.745
Hey!

01:01:05.828 --> 01:01:06.829
I said she's bleeding.

01:01:07.455 --> 01:01:08.289
Right.

01:01:09.165 --> 01:01:11.876
If there's bleeding, quickly recognize it…

01:01:12.585 --> 01:01:13.670
Quickly…

01:01:13.753 --> 01:01:14.921
-Place the line.
-Okay.

01:01:16.297 --> 01:01:17.882
I did the SPEED CP, so…

01:01:17.965 --> 01:01:20.551
TIME-SENSITIVE PROTOCOL FOR MANAGING PPH

01:01:21.969 --> 01:01:24.180
Nurse, please insert the Foley.

01:01:24.764 --> 01:01:26.307
Then…

01:01:27.684 --> 01:01:29.644
Right, mix oxytocin into the fluids.

01:01:29.727 --> 01:01:32.021
-And give an IV push of carbetocin.
-Yes, Doctor.

01:01:32.605 --> 01:01:34.691
-Are the labs on their way?
-Yes, they are.

01:01:38.528 --> 01:01:41.072
Doctor, please set up
the rapid infusion system.

01:01:41.155 --> 01:01:42.281
Okay.

01:01:42.907 --> 01:01:45.284
-Give the fluids at full drip.
-Yes, Doctor.

01:01:45.368 --> 01:01:46.285
It's open.

01:01:46.369 --> 01:01:47.203
Nam-kyung.

01:01:50.581 --> 01:01:51.958
Get it together!

01:01:54.877 --> 01:01:56.462
I'm scared too!

01:01:59.841 --> 01:02:01.175
Right.

01:02:02.719 --> 01:02:03.970
Remove the balloon first.

01:02:16.107 --> 01:02:17.024
The OR.

01:02:25.950 --> 01:02:28.244
This is OB. Is the OR ready?

01:02:28.828 --> 01:02:30.413
Please hurry! It's urgent!

01:02:33.040 --> 01:02:33.916
-Nurse.
-Yes?

01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:35.084
I called the blood bank.

01:02:35.168 --> 01:02:37.587
Get two packs of universal O first

01:02:37.670 --> 01:02:39.589
-and send it straight to the OR.
-Yes, Doctor!

01:02:39.672 --> 01:02:40.631
-Hurry!
-Okay!

01:02:42.008 --> 01:02:43.634
Doctor, please place an A-line as well.

01:02:43.718 --> 01:02:44.594
Okay.

01:02:47.096 --> 01:02:51.184
EMERGENCY MEDICINE

01:02:56.647 --> 01:02:57.899
-Doctor.
-Yes?

01:02:57.982 --> 01:02:59.734
The patient has a history of DDLT.

01:02:59.817 --> 01:03:01.527
-What?
-Oh, right.

01:03:01.611 --> 01:03:05.448
We'll need the liver transplant team
to help check the lab results,

01:03:05.531 --> 01:03:06.699
but they're not here.

01:03:08.618 --> 01:03:10.369
Give it to me. I'll take a look.

01:03:10.870 --> 01:03:11.704
Here.

01:03:13.539 --> 01:03:15.082
I'm an HPB surgeon from Songdo Yulje.

01:03:15.166 --> 01:03:16.459
I'll take a look.

01:03:17.001 --> 01:03:19.504
How long ago did she have the transplant?

01:03:19.587 --> 01:03:21.380
It's been seven years.

01:03:21.464 --> 01:03:22.965
And she gave birth two years ago.

01:03:24.008 --> 01:03:25.301
Her liver enzymes are normal.

01:03:25.927 --> 01:03:29.514
Use antibiotics general patients get,
and she can go in for surgery now.

01:03:30.473 --> 01:03:32.600
There might be some adhesion,
so be careful.

01:03:32.683 --> 01:03:33.518
Quickly, now.

01:03:34.143 --> 01:03:35.603
-Thank you!
-Thank you!

01:03:36.270 --> 01:03:37.271
Moving her now.

01:03:41.317 --> 01:03:43.152
Bed coming through! Please make way!

01:03:50.284 --> 01:03:52.161
Ma'am, please wake up!

01:03:52.245 --> 01:03:53.329
Please!

01:03:53.412 --> 01:03:55.039
I'm so sleepy.

01:03:55.122 --> 01:03:56.999
No, you can't sleep! Open your eyes!

01:03:58.376 --> 01:03:59.252
Ma'am!

01:03:59.335 --> 01:04:00.545
Ma'am!

01:04:01.128 --> 01:04:02.421
It's your baby's birthday today!

01:04:03.506 --> 01:04:05.508
So the baby's waiting for its mom.

01:04:05.591 --> 01:04:06.592
We have to go to it.

01:04:07.343 --> 01:04:08.177
Right.

01:04:18.771 --> 01:04:20.523
-Anesthesia, please.
-Yes, Doctor.

01:04:26.487 --> 01:04:27.655
The patient's a multi, right?

01:04:27.738 --> 01:04:28.865
Yes, she is.

01:04:28.948 --> 01:04:30.533
She delivered two and a half hours ago.

01:04:30.616 --> 01:04:31.701
They said the baby's fine.

01:04:31.784 --> 01:04:32.702
Bleeding volume?

01:04:32.785 --> 01:04:35.371
I think it's been
about 2,000 cc until now.

01:04:35.454 --> 01:04:38.791
The speculum exam in the ER
showed active bleeding.

01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:40.251
How much blood did she get?

01:04:40.334 --> 01:04:43.880
She got one unit in the helicopter,
so a total of three so far.

01:04:43.963 --> 01:04:45.298
We got two universal O units,

01:04:45.381 --> 01:04:46.799
and we prepped ten RBC

01:04:46.883 --> 01:04:48.801
and five units of FFP from the bank.

01:04:49.719 --> 01:04:50.761
When will they be ready?

01:04:51.262 --> 01:04:53.180
It'll take about 20 minutes.

01:04:53.264 --> 01:04:55.892
Are the CBC and DIC labs back?

01:04:55.975 --> 01:05:00.521
Yes, labs sent from the ER show
CBC 6.2, and platelets 90,000.

01:05:01.230 --> 01:05:02.815
OTPT is normal.

01:05:02.899 --> 01:05:04.150
And they say PT and aPTT

01:05:04.734 --> 01:05:06.986
seem to be prolonged.

01:05:07.695 --> 01:05:10.114
The other DIC labs are still in progress.

01:05:10.197 --> 01:05:11.866
Good job. You did very well!

01:05:12.575 --> 01:05:14.076
Dr. Pyo, scrub in first!

01:05:16.704 --> 01:05:17.538
I can't.

01:05:18.414 --> 01:05:19.415
Then, Yi-young!

01:05:21.834 --> 01:05:23.878
You're both assisting! Get it together!

01:05:23.961 --> 01:05:25.046
The patient's--

01:05:25.129 --> 01:05:26.213
Move aside, guys.

01:05:26.714 --> 01:05:27.715
What about your surgery?

01:05:27.798 --> 01:05:28.799
It's over.

01:05:28.883 --> 01:05:31.552
Professor, the patient…

01:05:31.636 --> 01:05:33.679
I know. I'm looking at her right now.

01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:43.064
Hey, we have no one assisting today.

01:05:43.147 --> 01:05:44.398
It appears we don't.

01:05:44.482 --> 01:05:46.442
All we can count on is our team.

01:05:48.778 --> 01:05:51.155
BP's dropping! It's 70 over 40!

01:05:51.238 --> 01:05:53.866
We'll keep up with the volume,
so don't worry and start.

01:05:56.243 --> 01:05:58.287
Yes, we'll begin now.

01:06:12.635 --> 01:06:14.553
ANESTHESIA TIME, SURGERY TIME

01:06:18.808 --> 01:06:20.142
Kelly.

01:06:23.646 --> 01:06:25.231
-One more Kelly.
-Yes, ma'am.

01:06:27.191 --> 01:06:28.067
Metzenbaum.

01:06:29.318 --> 01:06:30.736
Prepare the 1-0 suture tie.

01:06:37.076 --> 01:06:38.244
Tie.

01:06:45.001 --> 01:06:46.002
Cut.

01:06:50.381 --> 01:06:51.799
Tranexamic acid, please.

01:06:51.882 --> 01:06:52.883
Yes, Professor.

01:07:05.187 --> 01:07:06.063
Tonsil.

01:07:09.859 --> 01:07:10.693
Right angle.

01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:18.159
Hold the suction!

01:07:18.242 --> 01:07:19.368
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

01:07:43.517 --> 01:07:46.353
I was worried about severe adhesions
from the transplant,

01:07:46.437 --> 01:07:47.688
but things went smoothly.

01:07:47.772 --> 01:07:49.732
I know. It's a relief.

01:07:53.027 --> 01:07:54.111
What do you think?

01:07:55.863 --> 01:07:57.114
She's not bleeding.

01:07:57.198 --> 01:07:58.115
And?

01:08:00.076 --> 01:08:00.993
The patient's…

01:08:03.829 --> 01:08:05.081
alive.

01:08:05.164 --> 01:08:06.540
The patient

01:08:07.792 --> 01:08:09.543
can meet her baby.

01:08:10.711 --> 01:08:11.754
No, not that!

01:08:12.338 --> 01:08:16.342
Blood loss was 4,000 cc,
but her vitals are stable.

01:08:18.219 --> 01:08:20.304
Yes, that's right. It's stable.

01:08:20.387 --> 01:08:23.140
The operation went really well.

01:08:47.957 --> 01:08:48.833
Hey.

01:08:48.916 --> 01:08:49.917
What?

01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:51.669
Draft the surgery notes.

01:08:51.752 --> 01:08:53.963
Why me? Ask the juniors.

01:08:54.046 --> 01:08:56.215
They won't remember anything.

01:08:56.298 --> 01:08:58.884
I barely managed to rouse them
to come to their senses.

01:08:59.635 --> 01:09:00.678
Then you write it!

01:09:00.761 --> 01:09:02.263
You were there first.

01:09:02.346 --> 01:09:04.140
The assistant is supposed to write it!

01:09:04.765 --> 01:09:05.808
I was the lead surgeon.

01:09:06.725 --> 01:09:09.645
I was in such shock
that everything was a blur.

01:09:09.728 --> 01:09:12.356
Hey, you've been doing this too long
to still get shocked.

01:09:13.524 --> 01:09:14.984
PPH is nothing new.

01:09:15.067 --> 01:09:15.985
What about you?

01:09:16.485 --> 01:09:19.155
Hey, I realized it when I saw your hands.

01:09:19.238 --> 01:09:22.366
"So that's what it means
to shake like a leaf."

01:09:24.743 --> 01:09:27.121
If my hands were shaking,
my sutures wouldn't be so perfect.

01:09:27.204 --> 01:09:29.081
Perfect? Yeah, right.

01:09:29.165 --> 01:09:30.082
Hey, you two.

01:09:31.458 --> 01:09:34.086
Don't you think that's enough?

01:09:34.170 --> 01:09:37.173
All you have to say is,
"Thanks. Nice work."

01:09:37.256 --> 01:09:39.508
"You did great."

01:09:39.592 --> 01:09:43.053
But instead, you've been fighting
and arguing for 20 years.

01:09:43.137 --> 01:09:44.054
Gosh.

01:09:44.138 --> 01:09:45.556
Gosh, I'm so sick of it.

01:09:46.432 --> 01:09:47.766
I'm so tired of you two!

01:09:48.893 --> 01:09:49.727
Gosh.

01:09:56.901 --> 01:09:58.777
Nice work. Good job. Thanks. Happy?

01:09:59.695 --> 01:10:00.654
Don't be ridiculous.

01:10:00.738 --> 01:10:02.573
Gosh, I'm so sick of it.

01:10:04.241 --> 01:10:05.451
Geez, those two.

01:10:06.035 --> 01:10:06.869
Professor!

01:10:07.995 --> 01:10:09.580
Oh, dear. Their surgery's over.

01:10:09.663 --> 01:10:10.789
Sorry?

01:10:10.873 --> 01:10:12.708
The emergency OB surgery.

01:10:13.542 --> 01:10:14.501
It went well.

01:10:20.174 --> 01:10:21.717
Where are you going? Not going home?

01:10:24.094 --> 01:10:26.055
I'm coming into your surgery.

01:10:27.139 --> 01:10:29.516
It's laparoscopic.
Someone needs to control the manipulator.

01:10:31.310 --> 01:10:33.437
I was going to put it in place first.

01:10:33.520 --> 01:10:35.064
The fellow's running late.

01:10:35.564 --> 01:10:36.774
That's what I was going to do.

01:10:36.857 --> 01:10:38.776
I already told the fellow as well.

01:10:41.779 --> 01:10:43.280
It's all right. Go home.

01:10:43.864 --> 01:10:44.865
You had a long day.

01:10:47.076 --> 01:10:48.494
It's okay. Go.

01:10:48.577 --> 01:10:50.621
It's fine. I can do it fine alone too.

01:10:55.751 --> 01:10:57.253
But really, I'm fine.

01:11:00.839 --> 01:11:02.299
I'm fine too.

01:11:02.383 --> 01:11:03.801
I'd like to see you operate.

01:11:06.053 --> 01:11:07.596
Really?

01:11:07.680 --> 01:11:08.555
Is that so?

01:11:08.639 --> 01:11:10.849
Then do you want to try an RSO?
What do you think?

01:11:10.933 --> 01:11:12.643
Yes! Thank you!

01:11:12.726 --> 01:11:13.727
Really?

01:11:13.811 --> 01:11:15.646
Then we should…

01:11:15.729 --> 01:11:17.731
Yes, Professor. The patient's stable.

01:11:18.983 --> 01:11:20.901
I updated the air emergency team

01:11:20.985 --> 01:11:22.528
and thanked them as well.

01:11:24.655 --> 01:11:26.282
Yes, I'll monitor her closely.

01:11:27.950 --> 01:11:28.993
Okay, bye.

01:11:42.506 --> 01:11:43.340
Are you done?

01:11:44.550 --> 01:11:45.926
Can we have some more time?

01:11:46.510 --> 01:11:48.971
Doctor, it's not that we didn't do them.
We couldn't.

01:11:49.054 --> 01:11:49.930
Today, there was--

01:11:50.014 --> 01:11:50.848
I know.

01:11:53.267 --> 01:11:55.352
The patient asked me
to thank her doctors for her.

01:11:55.436 --> 01:11:58.022
The doctor who first spoke to her
when she landed

01:11:58.105 --> 01:12:00.482
and the doctor who mentioned
her baby's birthday party.

01:12:00.566 --> 01:12:01.400
That was you, right?

01:12:04.695 --> 01:12:07.531
You did a really great job today.

01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:11.327
I'm sure it was very scary,
difficult, and chaotic.

01:12:13.704 --> 01:12:17.249
So as a way to say you did well…

01:12:21.503 --> 01:12:22.463
I'll do the rest.

01:12:22.546 --> 01:12:23.380
What?

01:12:28.177 --> 01:12:29.053
No? Then, go ahead.

01:12:29.136 --> 01:12:30.721
No, that's not it.

01:12:33.640 --> 01:12:36.101
I'll count to three.
Go before I change my mind.

01:12:37.478 --> 01:12:38.645
One…

01:12:40.689 --> 01:12:42.608
-Bye!
-Thank you!

01:12:51.909 --> 01:12:53.118
See you there in two hours.

01:12:56.538 --> 01:12:59.291
Aren't you hungry?
You haven't eaten all day.

01:12:59.375 --> 01:13:00.542
Don't talk to me.

01:13:00.626 --> 01:13:02.044
I'm so hungry I can't even walk.

01:13:02.127 --> 01:13:02.961
Really?

01:13:03.712 --> 01:13:05.923
Do you want this then?
A nurse gave it to me.

01:13:06.507 --> 01:13:07.383
Here.

01:13:10.677 --> 01:13:11.929
There are only two.

01:13:12.012 --> 01:13:13.972
I bet the others haven't eaten either.

01:13:14.973 --> 01:13:15.891
Should we just…

01:13:17.976 --> 01:13:19.353
eat these ourselves before we go?

01:13:20.354 --> 01:13:22.815
Isn't that a bit selfish?

01:13:22.898 --> 01:13:24.691
These are really famous.

01:13:24.775 --> 01:13:27.361
They sell out daily,
and you have to wait in line.

01:13:28.404 --> 01:13:29.405
Still…

01:13:30.197 --> 01:13:31.573
Did you see them fight yesterday?

01:13:31.657 --> 01:13:32.491
Yeah.

01:13:32.574 --> 01:13:33.826
We have to leave them alone.

01:13:33.909 --> 01:13:36.203
They'll be too embarrassed
to make up with us there.

01:13:37.204 --> 01:13:39.790
Giving them space is to help them.

01:13:40.749 --> 01:13:41.625
Really?

01:13:43.001 --> 01:13:43.961
Then…

01:13:45.629 --> 01:13:46.505
Should we?

01:13:48.090 --> 01:13:49.174
Where should we eat?

01:13:50.551 --> 01:13:51.427
Let's go there.

01:13:52.428 --> 01:13:53.512
Oh, there?

01:13:53.595 --> 01:13:54.430
Yeah.

01:13:54.513 --> 01:13:56.140
I'm sure no one's there now. Let's go.

01:14:03.021 --> 01:14:04.648
I haven't been here in so long. Gosh.

01:14:04.731 --> 01:14:05.983
Maybe this isn't the way?

01:14:06.066 --> 01:14:06.984
Yeah, it is.

01:14:07.693 --> 01:14:10.821
If we turn left there and go straight,
there are escalators.

01:14:10.904 --> 01:14:12.573
We can take those down to the lobby.

01:14:14.700 --> 01:14:16.660
Song-hwa, how do you know everything?

01:14:18.162 --> 01:14:19.163
It says right there.

01:14:21.206 --> 01:14:22.249
I didn't see it.

01:14:22.332 --> 01:14:24.084
I was to busy looking at you.

01:14:26.420 --> 01:14:27.754
But you know,

01:14:27.838 --> 01:14:30.299
it's a bit scary
being on the outpatient floor at night.

01:14:31.133 --> 01:14:32.050
It's empty.

01:14:32.759 --> 01:14:33.594
No.

01:14:34.219 --> 01:14:35.429
There are people here.

01:14:37.806 --> 01:14:38.724
Who?

01:14:43.520 --> 01:14:45.439
There's no one here.
What are you talking about?

01:14:45.522 --> 01:14:47.316
Hey, don't do that!

01:14:47.399 --> 01:14:48.567
It's not scary.

01:14:49.401 --> 01:14:52.070
I'm sure there are roaches here.

01:14:52.154 --> 01:14:53.155
Roaches?

01:14:53.822 --> 01:14:55.574
Hospitals don't have roaches. No way.

01:14:55.657 --> 01:14:57.159
No, not real roaches.

01:14:58.494 --> 01:14:59.995
Dating roaches.

01:15:02.706 --> 01:15:03.707
They have no time

01:15:04.291 --> 01:15:05.375
and nowhere to meet.

01:15:05.459 --> 01:15:06.585
But they still need to date.

01:15:07.127 --> 01:15:10.756
So they only look
for empty places in the hospital.

01:15:11.507 --> 01:15:13.342
So where do they all go?

01:15:14.468 --> 01:15:16.303
The emergency stairs? On-call rooms?

01:15:16.386 --> 01:15:19.014
Gosh, only if you want to get caught.

01:15:19.598 --> 01:15:20.474
Then where?

01:15:21.683 --> 01:15:22.768
Here?

01:15:25.187 --> 01:15:26.438
Exactly!

01:15:27.147 --> 01:15:29.816
There are no appointments,
patients, or staff here at night.

01:15:30.943 --> 01:15:34.196
So they secretly have dates here.

01:15:34.738 --> 01:15:37.366
But sometimes, professors come
to get things they left behind.

01:15:37.449 --> 01:15:38.575
Oh, no!

01:15:38.659 --> 01:15:40.869
-When they enter and turn on the lights…
-Yeah?

01:15:40.953 --> 01:15:43.288
They scatter and disappear like roaches.

01:15:43.372 --> 01:15:44.498
Where do they all go?

01:15:44.581 --> 01:15:48.710
Well, they cling to the wall
or hide behind the door.

01:15:48.794 --> 01:15:50.546
Or they hide under the desk.

01:15:54.341 --> 01:15:55.384
But

01:15:56.718 --> 01:15:58.470
how do you know about this so well?

01:16:01.765 --> 01:16:03.225
You've done a lot of hiding before?

01:16:04.851 --> 01:16:05.727
What are you…

01:16:06.520 --> 01:16:08.355
Hey, it was Jun-wan.

01:16:09.273 --> 01:16:12.693
When he was a resident,
he did it a lot. I heard it from him.

01:16:16.697 --> 01:16:17.864
I wonder if anyone's here.

01:16:19.491 --> 01:16:20.951
Hey, don't!

01:16:23.996 --> 01:16:25.330
This isn't even our hospital.

01:16:27.416 --> 01:16:28.333
Do you hear something?

01:16:29.585 --> 01:16:30.669
I think I hear something.

01:16:32.504 --> 01:16:33.380
What was that?

01:16:34.464 --> 01:16:35.465
I think someone knocked.

01:16:35.549 --> 01:16:37.259
I don't hear anything.

01:16:37.342 --> 01:16:39.219
-No one's here.
-Did you do that, Song-hwa?

01:16:40.053 --> 01:16:41.054
You scared me.

01:16:41.680 --> 01:16:42.639
Let's go.

01:16:43.181 --> 01:16:44.391
I'll let you off today.

01:16:45.350 --> 01:16:48.228
But I don't think young people these days
would come here.

01:16:48.770 --> 01:16:51.732
They all hold hands
and get coffee together out in the open.

01:16:51.815 --> 01:16:53.442
That's only the tip of the iceberg.

01:16:53.525 --> 01:16:55.319
Gosh, Song-hwa.

01:16:55.861 --> 01:16:57.863
You know how many date in secret here?

01:16:58.530 --> 01:17:00.282
It's 520.

01:17:02.200 --> 01:17:04.286
Hey, don't.
What if someone's really in there?

01:17:08.874 --> 01:17:10.459
See?

01:17:10.542 --> 01:17:11.710
It's all in the past.

01:17:12.461 --> 01:17:14.421
Gen Z doesn't do that these days.

01:17:15.422 --> 01:17:16.632
I'm not sure about that.

01:17:16.715 --> 01:17:19.217
Even last year, I caught a lot of them.

01:17:20.969 --> 01:17:22.804
I guess there are no roaches here.

01:17:24.139 --> 01:17:25.390
What should we have for dinner?

01:17:25.474 --> 01:17:27.893
The guys want us
to come quick for your discharge party.

01:17:27.976 --> 01:17:30.020
-They want ramyeon.
-Should we get some kimbap…

01:17:32.814 --> 01:17:33.857
You told the guys?

01:17:33.940 --> 01:17:36.234
Look, I really wasn't going to tell them.

01:17:36.985 --> 01:17:38.654
But they kept asking where we were

01:17:38.737 --> 01:17:40.656
and when we were coming back,
and eventually--

01:17:40.739 --> 01:17:42.699
That means everyone at the hospital knows.

01:17:43.325 --> 01:17:44.451
I'm sorry.

01:17:45.452 --> 01:17:47.704
I should've just gone to our hospital.

01:17:47.788 --> 01:17:50.165
I came all the way to Jongno,
and now everyone knows.

01:17:52.626 --> 01:17:53.460
You're right.

01:17:55.712 --> 01:17:57.589
But are you really okay now?

01:17:58.340 --> 01:17:59.633
No, I'm not okay.

01:18:00.258 --> 01:18:02.678
My hands are still burning hot
from all that praying.

01:18:02.761 --> 01:18:03.679
Do you feel the heat?

01:18:05.514 --> 01:18:07.974
You could've gotten seriously hurt though.

01:18:08.850 --> 01:18:10.394
Please be careful.

01:18:11.061 --> 01:18:13.772
The guys are going to make
so much fun of me.

01:18:15.148 --> 01:18:17.567
Why did they leave this door open?

01:18:18.694 --> 01:18:20.237
Shouldn't it be closed?

01:18:28.620 --> 01:18:29.579
They're gone.

01:18:31.873 --> 01:18:33.125
Geez, that was scary.

01:18:34.167 --> 01:18:35.043
But,

01:18:36.002 --> 01:18:36.837
why did we hide?

01:18:37.337 --> 01:18:38.213
What?

01:18:38.296 --> 01:18:39.631
Why did you tell me to hide?

01:18:39.715 --> 01:18:41.007
It's not like we can't be here.

01:18:42.509 --> 01:18:43.468
I told you to hide?

01:18:43.552 --> 01:18:46.096
Yeah, you pushed me under the desk.

01:18:47.305 --> 01:18:50.016
And you sat right next to me
and shushed me.

01:18:51.476 --> 01:18:52.310
I did?

01:18:54.730 --> 01:18:55.814
Why did I do that?

01:18:57.274 --> 01:18:58.608
Well, it was just in case…

01:19:00.944 --> 01:19:02.571
in case they scolded us for not working.

01:19:02.654 --> 01:19:03.530
But we're done.

01:19:03.613 --> 01:19:04.448
Right.

01:19:08.660 --> 01:19:12.956
Hey, even in a tense moment like that,
you could remember and argue every detail.

01:19:13.749 --> 01:19:14.916
Is it because you're smart?

01:19:22.674 --> 01:19:24.134
Oh, right. My gown!

01:19:33.059 --> 01:19:35.020
-Should I buy you some streusel bread?
-Yeah.

01:20:27.906 --> 01:20:30.242
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUESTS,
CHO JUNG-SEOK & JEON MI-DO,

01:20:30.325 --> 01:20:31.910
OUR ETERNAL LEE IK-JUN & CHAE SONG-HWA

01:20:32.452 --> 01:20:35.705
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:20:36.623 --> 01:20:37.749
The two of you? Where?

01:20:38.667 --> 01:20:39.918
What's this?

01:20:40.418 --> 01:20:42.295
-You're so cute.
-Dr. Ku?

01:20:42.379 --> 01:20:44.714
I have something big to tell you!

01:20:44.798 --> 01:20:46.758
Doctor, don't worry.

01:20:46.842 --> 01:20:48.844
I may not seem like it,
but I'm very loyal.

01:20:48.927 --> 01:20:51.388
Hello. I'm Yi-young's friend,
Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:20:51.471 --> 01:20:53.181
-These days, Yi-young is…
-Don't.

01:20:53.265 --> 01:20:55.517
There you go again.

01:20:55.600 --> 01:20:58.395
-Seong-chan.
-Yesterday, he was your dad and you wept.

01:20:58.478 --> 01:21:00.063
Today, he's your son?

01:21:00.146 --> 01:21:01.398
What are you doing?

01:21:01.481 --> 01:21:03.358
-You can't just touch that!
-Yi-young!

01:21:03.441 --> 01:21:05.735
Please, can't you just focus
on the contractions?

01:21:05.819 --> 01:21:07.779
-What?
-No, she can't go!

01:21:07.863 --> 01:21:09.364
The baby's umbilical cord is out!

01:21:09.447 --> 01:21:11.116
You can just come up right now yourself!

01:21:11.199 --> 01:21:12.742
-Quit staring!
-Professor?

01:21:13.451 --> 01:21:15.579
Do you remember my request?

01:21:15.662 --> 01:21:17.414
Well, if that's what you want…

01:21:17.497 --> 01:21:18.957
Yi-young, take the lead.

01:21:19.040 --> 01:21:20.208
Oh, my God.

01:21:20.292 --> 01:21:23.795
Do you think our age-old OB tradition
will work on Yi-young too?

01:21:23.879 --> 01:21:25.130
Where's Jae-il?

01:21:25.213 --> 01:21:26.131
Why go there at night?

01:21:26.214 --> 01:21:27.716
You're not dating.

01:21:27.799 --> 01:21:29.301
Does Jae-il like you?

01:21:29.384 --> 01:21:30.635
Are you two dating?

01:21:30.719 --> 01:21:32.512
Does he really like me?

01:21:39.728 --> 01:21:41.730
Subtitle translation by: Jamie Jin
